  "question": {
    "text": "The current flowing through the $1 \\Omega$ resistor is $\\frac{n}{10}$ A. The value of $n$ is _________\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0042_05489e22c43a.png\"><br>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "25",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0042_c807d1a8cac7.png\"><br />$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{y-5}{2}+\\frac{y-0}{2}+\\frac{y-x+10}{1}=0 \\\\ & y-5+y+2 y-2 x+20=0 \\\\ & 4 y-2 x+15=0 \\quad \\ldots .(\\text { (i) } \\\\ & \\frac{x-5}{4}+\\frac{x-0}{4}+\\frac{x-10-y}{1}=0 \\\\ & x-5+x+4 x-40-4 y=0 \\\\ & 6 x-4 y-45=0 \\quad . .(i) \\\\ & \\frac{-2 x+4 y+15=0 . .(i i)}{4 x-30=0} \\\\ & x=\\frac{15}{2} \\& 4 y-15+15=0 \\\\ & y=0 \\\\ & i=\\frac{y-x+10}{1} \\\\ & i=\\frac{0-7.5+10}{1} \\\\ & i=2.5 A=\\frac{n}{10} A \\\\ & n=25\\end{aligned}$"
  }
